course: dictionary
lesson: 14012
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change meaning depending on the sentence. «Dad got madder when the dog dug up the flowers.» Here madder is the -er form of mad, so it means more angry. The -er ending makes the feeling stronger.
explain: In UK English, mad often means crazy or silly, not angry. «The twins were madder than ever at the party, giggling and running in circles.» Here madder means wilder and sillier. Look at the clues: giggling and running in circles tell you it is silly fun, not anger.
explain: Madder can also be a noun, the name of a plant. «The painter mixed madder to make a deep red for the old picture.» Here madder is not about feelings at all. The plant's roots gave a red dye, and the clues are mixed and red. When a word has several meanings, try each one in the sentence and pick the one that makes sense.
fact: Madder is the -er form of mad, so it means more mad: «He got madder and madder.»
fact: In American English, mad usually means angry, so madder means more angry.
fact: In UK English, mad often means crazy or silly, as in «mad about football», which means loves football very much.
fact: Madder is also a plant whose roots give a red dye, used for thousands of years to colour cloth.
fact: A good check is to swap in a meaning: if angry, silly or red fits the sentence, you have found the right one.
exercise: «Dad got madder and madder when the dog dug up the garden.» What does madder mean here? | *More angry | Lost in the garden | Better at sport | Very happy
exercise: «The twins were madder than ever, giggling and running in circles.» What does madder mean here, in UK English? | *More crazy or silly | Angrier with the twins | More tired | Quieter
exercise: «The painter mixed madder to make a deep red for the old picture.» What is madder here? | A type of paintbrush | A red coat | A kind of dog | *A plant whose roots give a red dye
test: Madder is the -er form of which word? | Madness | Madam | Made | *Mad
test: «She mixed rose madder to paint the sunset.» What is madder in this sentence? | Blue paint | Very angry | *A red dye from a plant | A kind of cake
exam: In «He was madder than the wasp that stung him», what does madder mean? | A plant with red roots | Redder | Wilder and sillier | *More angry
